{%- comment -%}
  Live Group Buy progress (README "Live Savings / Progress").

  WHAT THIS BLOCK DOES NOT DO, and why that is the interesting part:

  - It shows NO crowdfunding-style "% funded" bar. A percentage-of-goal reads
    as money raised towards a target that must be met, and a Group Buy has no
    target. The README forbids it outright. The progress indicator here marks
    TIER THRESHOLDS on a track, which communicates "the price drops at 10" —
    not "we are 40% of the way to being allowed to proceed".
  - It never implies a minimum. One qualifying unit already buys at Tier 1, so
    the copy is always "the price drops at N" and never "N more needed to
    unlock this campaign".

  RENDERS NOTHING UNTIL IT HAS REAL DATA. No placeholder prices, no skeleton
  numbers. A price that appears and then changes is worse than one that appears
  a moment later, because the first version is a claim we cannot honour.

  All values come from the app's App Proxy endpoint, which is the single source
  of the campaign's live state. Nothing about tiers or prices is computed here:
  a template that did its own arithmetic would be a second place a
  customer-facing price is decided.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign campaign_code = block.settings.campaign_code | strip
  assign selected_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
-%}

{%- if campaign_code != blank -%}
  <div
    class="carat-gb"
    data-carat-group-buy
    data-campaign-code="{{ campaign_code | escape }}"
    data-variant-id="{{ selected_variant.id }}"
    data-money-format="{{ shop.money_format | escape }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {%- comment -%}
      aria-live so a shopper using a screen reader hears the price when it
      arrives, and hears it again when the tier changes — this region updates
      without a page load, which is otherwise silent.
      `polite` rather than `assertive`: a price update should not interrupt.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div
      class="carat-gb__body"
      data-carat-gb-body
      aria-live="polite"
      aria-busy="true"
      hidden
    ></div>

    <p class="carat-gb__loading" data-carat-gb-loading>
      {{ 'group_buy.loading' | t }}
    </p>

    {%- comment -%}
      No-JS and failure both land here. Saying plainly that group pricing is
      unavailable is better than leaving an empty box that looks broken, or —
      far worse — showing the Buy Now price as if it were the group price.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <noscript>
      <p class="carat-gb__unavailable">{{ 'group_buy.unavailable' | t }}</p>
    </noscript>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{{ 'group-buy-progress.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'group-buy-progress.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Group Buy progress",
  "target": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "campaign_code",
      "label": "Campaign code",
      "info": "The Group Buy campaign code from the CaratForUs admin. Leave blank to hide this block."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
